# Injected into every `bun test` run so the suite's verdict never depends on whether it was
# started inside a subagent (pi-config#22, owner 2026-11-20). Bun sets NODE_ENV=test for
# `bun test` and loads this file into the env snapshot taken at process start — the snapshot a
# child spawned without `env` receives — so the injected values reach spawns, not only in-process
# readers. A real environment variable wins over this file, so a subagent's own run is unchanged.
#
# Values are the harness's (extensions/subagent-async): an allowlist that refuses the
# `implement`/`orchestrator` spawns the boundary rows are about, and a depth that counts against
# the cap. A file whose rows are not about env control scrubs them in `beforeAll`
# (tests/helpers/subagent-env.ts); a file that makes billed model calls must scrub too, which
# tests/subagent-boundary-hermeticity.test.ts pins.
PI_SUBAGENT_ALLOWLIST=review-code,review-tests
PI_SUBAGENT_DEPTH=1
PI_IS_SUBAGENT=1
